From dcdf2a1629132e98cdba8de37715fadafcc70691 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 18:53:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 53/54] [AGS] Wire type-5 MIDI clips into midi_sched + the OPL3
 sink (Sound milestone S4)

sound.cpp's load_sound_clip() now sniffs the real SMF header magic
("MThd") on every clip small enough to load whole -- a Standard MIDI File
is always tiny, so it is always on that branch, never the streamed one --
same convention S1's own RIFF/VOC PCM loader already established (a
v361_objnames-era game's fileName/fileType pairing is not reliable,
PLAN.md's own research). A real MIDI clip now routes to the new
audio_core_slot_init_midi() instead of the PCM audio_core_slot_init(),
and forces soundType=MUS_MIDI regardless of what ext_hint said, since
SoundClip::posms_to_pos()/pos_to_posms() branch on it.

audio_core_slot_init_midi() writes the clip's raw SMF bytes to a fixed
scratch DOS path (DOSMIDI.TMP, binary fopen) -- midi_sched_open() reads a
file, not a memory buffer, and AGS's music channel is a single reserved
slot (SCHAN_MUSIC), so only one MIDI clip is ever live at a time; a fixed
filename is sufficient. Unlike the PCM overloads, this never fails to
init a slot: even a chip-less/backend-less session gets a real AudioPlayer
whose Init() reports PlayStateError honestly, matching the existing
"AudioClip.Play: unable to load sound file" precedent a missing PCM
decoder already produces.

AudioPlayer gains a second, MIDI-mode constructor (PLAN.md's own framing:
"the music channel's AudioPlayer becomes a thin adapter") driving a
midi_sched + opl3_sink pair instead of SDLDecoder/OpenAlSource -- every
method (Poll/Play/Pause/Stop/Seek/Get*/Set*) branches on _isMidi
internally, so SoundClip (soundclip.cpp) needed zero changes: it only
ever calls these same methods via audio_core_get_player(slot). MIDI has
no PCM bytes to decode (OPL3 output is direct hardware register writes,
never an SDL3 stream), so forcing it through the PCM-shaped
SDLDecoder/OpenAlSource interface was never the right shape here.

Notable design points, not just mechanical translation:
- A dedicated MidiNowMs() (uclock()-based, same epoch every other
  DOS-PORT timestamp in this engine uses) minus an accumulated pause
  offset gives Pause()->Play() a continuous, pause-aware clock --
  midi_sched_start() only knows how to arm from the song start, not
  resume from an arbitrary position, so without this a pause would make
  the schedule jump forward by however long the game was paused.
- Stop() has no shared-layer "silence everything, keep the chip open"
  entry point available (opl3_sink.h only exposes per-note NOTE_OFF via a
  real MIDI event, or a full close() that unconditionally KEY-OFFs all 18
  voices) -- reuses close()/reopen to guarantee a stopped clip never
  leaves a note physically hanging, at the cost of a redundant chip
  re-detect on the next Play().
- GetFrequency/GetDurationMs/GetPositionMs return 0 for MIDI (matching
  soundType==MUS_MIDI's pre-existing "TODO: reimplement" precedent in
  posms_to_pos/pos_to_posms) and Seek() is a no-op, per PLAN.md's own
  decision ("seek/position 0, upstream-equivalent") -- deliberately not
  adopting midi_sched_position_ms() for a real value here even though it
  exists, to match that decision rather than second-guess it.
- SetVolume/SetPanning/SetSpeed are tracked-but-unapplied/no-op for MIDI
  (opl3_sink.c's own sink_control_change() does not implement CC7/
  expression at this scope) -- same "tracked but never applied" precedent
  OpenAlSource::SetSpeed() already established for the PCM path's own
  un-implemented resampling.
- midi_sched_tick() loops the song from the start at end-of-song
  unconditionally (its own documented behavior) -- a MIDI AudioPlayer
  never reaches PlayStateFinished on its own, matching how background
  music is actually used; only an explicit Stop() ends playback.

Verified under DOSBox-X (oplmode=opl3, a scratch conf copy -- this hub's
own shared confs default oplmode=none and were not touched): AGS Quest's
full 18-phase + optional-dialog sequence stays ok, all 3 screenshots stay
byte-identical to the existing baseline, PCM underruns=0 (matching S1/S2,
zero regression), audio_vital_status reads
"midi=opl3,events=29" -- real dispatch through the actual OPL3 register
I/O path, not just a parse-only witness. Also verified clean under the
stock oplmode=none conf (no chip): "midi=none,events=0", exit_code=0, all
phases/screenshots still pass -- the fail-closed path is not a regression
risk for every port/environment that has no OPL3 hardware.

